d 'XTGFE': module to perform grouped fixed-effects (GFE) estimation for panel data (Bonhomme and Manresa, 2015)
d
d  xtgfe estimates the grouped fixed-effects model of Bonhomme and
d Manresa (2015, Econometrica), in which the units of a panel are
d classified into a finite number of latent groups, each with its
d own time-varying (or, optionally, time-invariant) fixed effect.
d Group membership is unobserved and is estimated from the data,
d jointly with the common coefficients. Both of the authors'
d computational algorithms are implemented (the iterative Algorithm
d 1 and the variable neighborhood search Algorithm 2), for balanced
d and unbalanced panels. Three types of standard errors are
d available: large-N large-T cluster-sandwich (default),
d unit-resampling bootstrap with bias correction, and the large-N
d fixed-T analytic formula based on Pollard (1982). The number of
d groups can be selected by the BIC criterion of the paper. 
d
d KW: grouped fixed effects
d KW: panel data
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260801
d
d Author: Ozan Eruygur,  Ankara Haci Bayram Veli University
d Support: email eruygur@@gmail.com
d
